title: The configuration repository
tags: Configuration
kind: reference
summary: What lives where under ~/.config/metafolder/ — one directory per program, plus scripts and docs.

`~/.config/metafolder/` (or `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/metafolder/`) is a git repository,
with one directory per program and two shared ones:

```
~/.config/metafolder/        a git repository (branches: default, main)
  .gitignore
  core/
    query-grammar            the simplified-query grammar (read by the clients)
    ignore-presets.toml      the named mf_ignore presets (read by the clients)
  daemon/
    config.toml              the repositories to load at startup, [settings]
    schema.default.json      the schema a new repository starts with
  gui/
    config.toml              ports, page sizes, panel defaults, …
    keybindings.toml         every keybinding
    style.css                the style sheet
    commands.js              your own GUI commands
    panel-types/<name>/      the panel types, shipped and yours
  cli/
    config.toml              [settings], a default [repo], [tag]
  scripts/                   the shipped helper scripts (script:run)
  docs/                      this documentation, rendered (the help panel reads it)
```

The programs read `main`'s working tree, and only it; they never run git. Only
`metafolder-sync-config` does ([[Updating the configuration]]).

The per-program files: [[Daemon configuration]], [[GUI configuration]], [[CLI configuration]],
[[Slow log configuration]] (daemon and GUI). `docs/` is the one directory that is
a build product rather than a source file.
